{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"buzzers","name":"Buzzers and a microphone","version":"1.1.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"An active buzzer (beeps by itself when powered), a passive buzzer (plays the note you give it with tone()) and a sound sensor (KY-038 microphone module) that hears what parts on the bench play. You hear the buzzers too: the toolbar's Sound button turns part sounds on and off (the microphone hears them either way).","category":"Sound","needsApp":"0.4.0","code":"// Buzzers. An active one has its own oscillator: DC on its + makes it beep at its own pitch. A\n// passive one is just a little speaker: it sounds at whatever frequency its + is switched at\n// (tone() is PWM at that frequency), and a steady level only clicks once.\n\nbench.device('active-buzzer', (part) => {\n  const snd = part.sound();\n  let on = false, volts = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      volts = io.supply('+', '-');\n      const p = io.pwm('+');\n      // driven by tone(): its oscillator gets chopped, which sounds rough (as a real one does)\n      const level = p ? p.duty : 1;\n      on = volts > 2.5 && level > 0.05;\n      if (on) snd.tone(2300, Math.min(1, (volts / 5) * (p ? 0.6 : 0.8)), p ? 'sawtooth' : 'square');\n      else snd.stop();\n      io.draw(on ? 0.025 : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      return [on ? `beeping (${volts.toFixed(1)} V)` : volts > 0.5 ? `quiet (${volts.toFixed(1)} V is too little)` : 'quiet'];\n    },\n  };\n});\n\nbench.device('passive-buzzer', (part) => {\n  const snd = part.sound();\n  let hz = 0, volts = 0, clickUntil = -1, lastLevel = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      const p = io.pwm('+');\n      volts = (io.v('+') ?? 0) - (io.v('-') ?? 0);\n      const level = io.level('+') ?? 0;\n      if (p && p.hz >= 20 && volts > 0.5) {\n        hz = p.hz;\n        snd.tone(hz, Math.min(1, volts / 5) * Math.min(1, p.duty * 2), 'square');\n      } else {\n        hz = 0;\n        // a steady level only moves its disc once: a click\n        if (level !== lastLevel) clickUntil = io.time + 0.01;\n        if (io.time < clickUntil) snd.tone(180, 0.3, 'square');\n        else snd.stop();\n      }\n      lastLevel = level;\n      io.draw(hz ? 0.015 : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      return [hz ? `playing ${Math.round(hz)} Hz` : 'quiet (it needs tone(pin, frequency))'];\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n// Sound sensor (KY-038): a microphone and an amplifier. It hears what parts on the bench play\n// (part.hear(): 0..1 loudness, closer is louder). AO sits at VCC/2 in quiet and swings with the sound\n// (here: its average swing, rising with loudness); DO is HIGH while louder than the pot's setting.\nbench.device('sound-sensor', (part) => {\n  const ear = part.hear();\n  const threshold = Number(part.params.threshold ?? 20) / 100;\n  let powered = false, level = 0, loud = false, hz = 0, peaks = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      powered = v >= 2.5;\n      level = ear.level;\n      hz = ear.hz;\n      const now = level > threshold;\n      if (now && !loud) peaks++;\n      loud = now;\n      if (!powered) { io.release('AO'); io.release('DO'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      io.drive('AO', v * Math.min(1, 0.5 + level * 0.5), 1);\n      io.drive('DO', loud ? v : 0, 1);\n      io.draw(0.004 + (loud ? 0.002 : 0));\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      return [level > 0.002 ? `hears ${Math.round(level * 100)} %${hz ? ` (${hz} Hz)` : ''}${loud ? ': DO HIGH' : ''}` : 'quiet', `${peaks} loud moments`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","parts":[{"id":"active-buzzer","name":"Active buzzer","description":"Beeps (about 2.3 kHz) whenever + is above 2.5 V: digitalWrite(pin, HIGH) to beep, LOW to stop. Long leg + to a pin, short leg - to GND. A tone() on it just sounds rough: it has its own oscillator.","swatch":"#1c1c1e","mass":2,"sound":true,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.6,0.9],"at":[0,0.45,0],"color":"#1c1c1e"},{"cyl":[0.12,0.02],"at":[0,0.91,0],"color":"#0a0a0a","collide":false},{"box":[0.5,0.01,0.12],"at":[0,0.905,-0.3],"color":"#f2f2f2","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"+","label":"+ (long leg)","at":[-0.25,0,0],"kind":"in"},{"id":"-","label":"- (short leg)","at":[0.25,0,0],"kind":"gnd"}],"device":"active-buzzer"},{"id":"passive-buzzer","name":"Passive buzzer","description":"Plays the frequency it's driven at: tone(pin, 440) is an A, noTone(pin) stops. A plain HIGH only clicks. + to a pin, - to GND.","swatch":"#14361f","mass":2,"sound":true,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.6,0.8],"at":[0,0.4,0],"color":"#1c1c1e"},{"box":[1.3,0.08,1.3],"at":[0,0.04,0],"color":"#1d6b3a"},{"cyl":[0.15,0.02],"at":[0,0.81,0],"color":"#0a0a0a","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"+","label":"+ (signal)","at":[-0.25,0,0],"kind":"in"},{"id":"-","label":"-","at":[0.25,0,0],"kind":"gnd"}],"device":"passive-buzzer"},{"id":"sound-sensor","name":"Sound sensor (KY-038)","description":"A microphone with an amplifier: AO follows how loud it is (about VCC/2 when quiet, swinging wider when loud), DO goes HIGH while it's louder than the pot's setting. It hears the buzzers and speakers on the bench: closer is louder. VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, DO, AO.","swatch":"#c83030","mass":3,"params":[{"key":"threshold","label":"Pot: loud above (0-100)","kind":"number","min":1,"max":100,"step":1}],"defaults":{"threshold":20},"hear":true,"shape":[{"box":[1.5,0.16,3.6],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#c83030"},{"cyl":[0.5,0.5],"at":[0,0.41,1.3],"color":"#9aa0a8"},{"cyl":[0.4,0.02],"at":[0,0.67,1.3],"color":"#2b2b2e","collide":false},{"box":[0.6,0.45,0.6],"at":[0.3,0.38,-0.3],"color":"#3a70e0"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["AO","GND","VCC","DO"],"at":[-0.381,0,-1.65],"kinds":{"AO":"out","GND":"gnd","VCC":"vin","DO":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.5,"vmax":5.5},"AO":{"label":"AO (loudness)","analog":true},"DO":{"label":"DO (HIGH = loud)"}}}],"device":"sound-sensor"}],"examples":[{"name":"Play a tune","description":"A board playing a short tune on a passive buzzer with tone(), and beeping an active buzzer between the notes. Press Run (and turn Sound on).","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Play a tune","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"pz","type":"buzzers/passive-buzzer","name":"Passive buzzer","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[6,0,-2],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"az","type":"buzzers/active-buzzer","name":"Active buzzer","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[6,0,2],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"pz","pin":"+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"pz","pin":"-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP14"},"b":{"uid":"az","pin":"+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"az","pin":"-"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// A tune on the passive buzzer (tone plays a frequency), a beep on the active one between rounds.\n#define BUZZER 15\n#define BEEPER 14\n\nint melody[] = {262, 294, 330, 349, 392, 392, 440, 440, 392};\nint beats[]  = {1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 4};\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(BEEPER, OUTPUT);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  for (int i = 0; i < 9; i++) {\n    Serial.print(\"note \");\n    Serial.println(melody[i]);\n    tone(BUZZER, melody[i], beats[i] * 150);\n    delay(beats[i] * 200);\n  }\n  digitalWrite(BEEPER, HIGH);\n  delay(300);\n  digitalWrite(BEEPER, LOW);\n  delay(1000);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Hears the buzzer","description":"One board beeps a buzzer now and then; a sound sensor beside it hears each beep and lights an LED. Drag the buzzer further away and the beeps get too quiet to hear.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Hears the buzzer","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"buz","type":"buzzers/active-buzzer","name":"Buzzer","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,-5],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"mic","type":"buzzers/sound-sensor","name":"Sound sensor","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"led","type":"led","name":"Heard it","params":{"color":"green"},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,8],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"buz","pin":"+"},"color":"#e8c547","length":60},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"buz","pin":"-"},"color":"#2b2d33","length":60},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"mic","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"mic","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"mic","pin":"DO"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"A"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"K"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Hears the buzzer: a short beep every second and a half; the sound sensor beside it hears it and\n// the LED lights while it does. Drag the buzzer away: far off, the beeps are too quiet to hear.\n#define BUZZER 2\n#define HEARD 3     // the sound sensor's DO: HIGH while it's loud\n#define LED 15\n\nunsigned long nextBeep = 0;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(BUZZER, OUTPUT);\n  pinMode(HEARD, INPUT);\n  pinMode(LED, OUTPUT);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  if (millis() >= nextBeep) {\n    digitalWrite(BUZZER, HIGH);\n    delay(150);\n    digitalWrite(BUZZER, LOW);\n    nextBeep = millis() + 1500;\n  }\n  bool heard = digitalRead(HEARD) == HIGH;\n  digitalWrite(LED, heard ? HIGH : LOW);\n  if (heard) Serial.println(\"heard it!\");\n  delay(10);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}